  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 312 AM CDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nThe center of an upper level ridge shifts northeast of our region \nthrough the Long Term period. By the end of the period, the ridge\naxis is progged to reside near the Midwest and Great Lakes region,\nleaving our area on its west side. With ridging being our dominant\nweather maker, hot and mostly dry conditions remain in the forecast\nthrough the period. Highs each afternoon will range in the 90s to\ntriple digits. Highs beyond the century mark will mainly stay in \nthe northeastern Permian Basin, Eddy County, the Upper Trans \nPecos, and along the Rio Grande river valley. Overnight lows will \ncool to the 60s in and near the higher terrain, while 70s are \nforecast generally everywhere else. Rain chances mainly look slim \nto none through at least the middle of next week.",
